  "event_seq": 273,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to ~1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-02), not explained by response-time SLA breach (E-03) or a tariff change (E-04). Of 3025 disputed bills, the 1240 ESTIMATED-read bills (matching E-01 exactly) sit entirely on AMI read_channel accounts: 1184 (95.5%) had a valid pre-cutoff AMI read that was exported but rejected at billing import as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION (E-12). This is explained by validation rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01, which compares raw register values directly against 12-month m3 consumption history with unit_scaling='none' (E-13), while firmware v4.2 meters (rollout 2026-06) report registers in units of 0.1 m3 rather than m3 (E-14) — causing legitimate high-usage v4.2 reads to appear roughly 10x inflated and be wrongly rejected, forcing estimate substitution and incorrect bills for that cohort."
 },
